---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import Eyebrow from '../../components/Eyebrow.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="FAQ · Localis"
  description="Frequently asked questions about Localis audio guides: magic link, offline listening, refunds, AI voices and more."
  lang="en"
>
  <article class="max-w-narrow mx-auto px-md py-2xl">
    <Eyebrow class="mb-md">Frequently asked questions</Eyebrow>
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl text-ink mb-lg">FAQ</h1>

    <div class="prose prose-ink max-w-prose">

      <h2>How do I receive the guide after purchase?</h2>
      <p>
        Right after payment you'll receive an email with a permanent link (magic link). Open it on your phone, tablet, or computer — no app to download, no account to create. The link is yours forever.
      </p>

      <h2>Do I need internet to listen?</h2>
      <p>
        For streaming, yes: the guide is delivered in real time and requires a data connection or Wi-Fi. Coverage in Puglia is excellent in historic centres and along the main tourist routes.
      </p>

      <h2>Can I listen offline?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes, but you need to save it first. On your guide page (the one you receive by email) you'll find a <strong>Save for offline listening</strong> button. Tap it while connected: you'll see the download progress and, once complete, a <em>✓ Available offline</em> confirmation. From that point the guide works without a connection on that device. If you switch devices, you'll need to save it again.
      </p>

      <h2>Is the voice a real person or AI?</h2>
      <p>
        The voices are generated by a voice synthesiser (AI). The texts are written by local authors — people from Bari and Puglia who genuinely know these places. We chose synthetic voices because people who can describe an alley perfectly over coffee often freeze in front of a microphone. The stories are theirs; the voice is a tool. Full explanation on our <a href="/en/about">About page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How does the refund work?</h2>
      <p>
        1-click refund within 24 hours of purchase, no questions asked. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@localis.guide">hello@localis.guide</a> with your email address and the refund is processed the next business day.
      </p>

      <h2>Can I give a guide as a gift?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes. Buy with your email, then forward the magic link to the person you want to gift it to. The link works on any device, no sign-up required.
      </p>

      <h2>Is there a text transcript?</h2>
      <p>
        Not currently. The text is embedded in the audio narration. If you have accessibility needs, write to <a href="mailto:hello@localis.guide">hello@localis.guide</a> and we'll find a solution.
      </p>

      <h2>Does it work on iPhone and Android?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes, on any device with a modern browser (Safari, Chrome, Firefox). Nothing to install.
      </p>

      <h2>Can I listen at home before my trip?</h2>
      <p>
        Absolutely — it's one of the best ways to use it. Many listeners hear it on the sofa a few days before the trip, then replay it on location. The link never expires.
      </p>

      <h2>How long is a guide?</h2>
      <p>
        It depends on the guide. The Bari guides range from about 18 to 30 minutes. Valle d'Itria and Gargano guides are similar. The exact duration is shown on each guide's page.
      </p>

      <h2>Can I buy multiple guides together?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes — we offer bundles that group several guides at a reduced price. The Bari Complete bundle includes all 6 Bari guides and saves you €9.95 compared to buying them individually. You'll find them in the <a href="/en/#prezzi">Pricing section</a> on the homepage.
      </p>

      <h2>What languages are the guides available in?</h2>
      <p>
        Italian, English, and German. Each language version is written separately — not auto-translated. Not all guides are available in all languages yet; check the individual guide page for details.
      </p>

      <h2>Can I listen again after the trip?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes, the link is permanent. Many people replay guides after a trip to relive places or better understand what they saw.
      </p>

      <h2>Is the content verified?</h2>
      <p>
        Yes. Every claim in our guides has a source — historical archives, academic publications, local libraries. You can verify them all on the <a href="/en/fonti">Sources</a> page.
      </p>

      <h2>I can't find the answer I'm looking for. How do I contact you?</h2>
      <p>
        Write to <a href="mailto:hello@localis.guide">hello@localis.guide</a>. We reply within 24 hours on business days.
      </p>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
